+- 2026-10-24: sprinting, a port of Retro Sprint (periut; `retrosprint-master`, read in full: `ClientPlayerEntityMixin`, `LivingEntityMixin`, `PlayerEntityMixin`, `EntityMixin`, `GameRendererMixin*`, `WorldRendererMixin`, `BlockDustParticle`) (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +10 tests: `sprint::tests::*` (8), `mobs::tests::a_shove_is_halved_by_the_knockback_that_follows`, `gamepad::tests::l3_is_the_sprint_key`; run `cargo test --lib --release sprint mobs gamepad` first).
+    - `world/sprint.rs` (new, pure): `Sprint::tick` is `tickSprintingMovement` once per 20 Hz tick. Start: on the ground with forward held, the key (pad L3) sprints at once; otherwise the first press arms `sprintStartTicks` = 7 and a second press (forward released and pressed again, `bl3`) inside it sprints. Stop: forward released (sneaking scales it x0.3, so it ends a sprint too), a wall (`horizontalCollision`), water, riding, sleeping, dead, or 600 ticks after the start (`ticksSinceSprintingChanged`). Numbers: the push `ADD` = 0.035 / (1 - 0.546) blocks/tick = 1.54 m/s along the facing (settles at x1.35 of the walk, derived from the b1.7.3 drag, not measured), the jump push 0.2 blocks/tick that the air drag (x0.91) or the ground drag (x0.546) takes back down to `ADD`, field of view x1.15 by half the gap per tick (`fov_step`, frame-rate independent), hit shove 1.2 blocks/tick + 0.1 up.
+    - `lib.rs`: `sprint_tick` in the 20 Hz loop (forward = `touch.move_input.0`, x0.3 when sneaking; `ground` = `player.on_ground`; `blocked` = a frame since the last tick in which `physics::step` zeroed a horizontal velocity that was set; water = `was_in_water`); `step_frame` adds `sprint.add()` along the yaw to the walking velocity (the walk is set from the input every frame, so only the sprint's own part is added), fires `sprint.jump()` on a ground jump, scales the base field of view by `sprint.fov` (the look sensitivity divides it out again, so a sprint does not speed the look up), and `sprint_tick` throws one `Fx::Dig` speck of the block 0.2 under the feet per tick while it runs (`Effects::sprint_dust`: `-v * 4` sideways, 1.5 up, like `EntityMixin.addParticles`). A tap on a mob while sprinting calls `Mobs::shove` (the mod's `addVelocity` along the look, added before the hit's own `knockBack`, which halves it) and ends the sprint. Reset with the world and on respawn.
+    - `input/gamepad.rs` + `touch_ui.rs`: `Out::sprint` = L3 held, `TouchUi::pad_sprint`. L3 is fixed, not a `PadCfg` bind: the buttons page already fills its 6 rows (a 13th bind would sit on the `Tuning...` button). Touch needs no button: the d-pad's up arrow (or a corner: 0.707 counts as forward, `FWD_MIN` 0.7) tapped twice is the start.
